{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5,"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"accelerator":"GPU","colab":{"provenance":[],"gpuType":"T4","toc_visible":true}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# GVHMR on Colab \u2014 Track A fork\n","\n","Adapted from [`zju3dv/GVHMR`](https://github.com/zju3dv/GVHMR) `tools/demo/colab_demo.ipynb` (SIGGRAPH Asia 2024).\n","\n","**Why this copy exists:** the official notebook pins `torch==2.3.0+cu121`, a `pytorch3d` wheel for Python 3.10, and optionally compiles **DPVO**. Current Colab runtimes break on those pins. This notebook:\n","\n","- keeps Colab's preinstalled CUDA torch\n","- **does not compile DPVO** (use `-s` / SimpleVO)\n","- downloads the same public checkpoints the official notebook used\n","- exports `gvhmr_smpl.npz` for [`video-to-avatar-track-a`](https://github.com/m-mohsin-zafar/video-to-avatar-track-a) `scripts/ingest_smpl.py`\n","\n","Paper: [arXiv:2409.06662](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.06662) \u00b7 [project page](https://zju3dv.github.io/gvhmr)\n","\n","**Runtime \u2192 Change runtime type \u2192 T4 GPU.** If Colab asks to restart after pip, click **Cancel** and keep going.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. GPU check\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["# Runtime \u2192 Change runtime type \u2192 T4 GPU\n","!nvidia-smi\n","import sys, torch\n","print(\"python\", sys.version.split()[0])\n","print(\"torch\", torch.__version__, \"cuda\", torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else None)\n","assert torch.cuda.is_available(), \"No GPU. Runtime \u2192 Change runtime type \u2192 T4 GPU, then rerun.\"\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Install GVHMR (no DPVO, do not replace Colab torch)\n","\n","If a cell says \"restart runtime\", **Cancel**. Replacing torch is what kills the official notebook.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import os, sys\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","%cd /content\n","if not Path(\"/content/GVHMR\").exists():\n","    !git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/zju3dv/GVHMR /content/GVHMR\n","\n","proj_root = \"/content/GVHMR\"\n","%cd {proj_root}\n","\n","# requirements.txt pins torch 2.3+cu121 + a py3.10 pytorch3d wheel.\n","# Strip those lines and install the rest against Colab's torch.\n","req = Path(\"requirements.txt\").read_text().splitlines()\n","skip_prefixes = (\n","    \"--extra-index-url\",\n","    \"torch==\",\n","    \"torchvision==\",\n","    \"pytorch3d\",\n","    \"numpy==\",\n",")\n","filtered = []\n","for line in req:\n","    s = line.strip()\n","    if not s or s.startswith(\"#\"):\n","        continue\n","    if any(s.startswith(p) for p in skip_prefixes):\n","        print(\"skip pin:\", s)\n","        continue\n","    filtered.append(s)\n","\n","Path(\"/tmp/gvhmr_req_colab.txt\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(filtered) + \"\\n\")\n","print(\"--- installing ---\")\n","%pip install -q -r /tmp/gvhmr_req_colab.txt\n","%pip install -q -e .\n","\n","try:\n","    import pytorch3d\n","    print(\"pytorch3d\", pytorch3d.__version__)\n","except Exception:\n","    print(\"pytorch3d missing \u2014 will try a best-effort wheel next cell.\")\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["try:\n","    import pytorch3d\n","    print(\"pytorch3d already present\", getattr(pytorch3d, \"__version__\", \"\"))\n","except Exception:\n","    print(\"trying pip pytorch3d (may fail; inference still works)\")\n","    try:\n","        %pip install -q pytorch3d\n","    except Exception as exc:\n","        print(\"pytorch3d pip failed \u2014 continue anyway:\", exc)\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Checkpoints\n","\n","Same files the official notebook pulled from Hugging Face mirrors (`camenduru/GVHMR`, `camenduru/SMPLer-X`).\n","\n","SMPL / SMPL-X body models are **MPI-licensed**. By downloading you agree to the [SMPL](https://smpl.is.tue.mpg.de/) and [SMPL-X](https://smpl-x.is.tue.mpg.de/) terms. Do not commit these files to GitHub.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","proj_root = \"/content/GVHMR\"\n","%cd {proj_root}\n","!mkdir -p inputs outputs\n","\n","!apt-get install -y -qq aria2 >/dev/null\n","\n","def fetch(url, dest_dir, name):\n","    Path(dest_dir).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","    out = Path(dest_dir) / name\n","    if out.exists() and out.stat().st_size > 1000:\n","        print(\"have\", out)\n","        return\n","    !aria2c --console-log-level=error -c -x 16 -s 16 -k 1M \"{url}\" -d \"{dest_dir}\" -o \"{name}\"\n","\n","base_s = \"https://huggingface.co/camenduru/SMPLer-X/resolve/main\"\n","base_g = \"https://huggingface.co/camenduru/GVHMR/resolve/main\"\n","\n","fetch(f\"{base_s}/SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl\", \"inputs/checkpoints/body_models/smpl\", \"SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl\")\n","fetch(f\"{base_s}/SMPLX_NEUTRAL.npz\", \"inputs/checkpoints/body_models/smplx\", \"SMPLX_NEUTRAL.npz\")\n","fetch(f\"{base_g}/gvhmr/gvhmr_siga24_release.ckpt\", \"inputs/checkpoints/gvhmr\", \"gvhmr_siga24_release.ckpt\")\n","fetch(f\"{base_g}/hmr2/epoch%3D10-step%3D25000.ckpt\", \"inputs/checkpoints/hmr2\", \"epoch=10-step=25000.ckpt\")\n","fetch(f\"{base_g}/vitpose/vitpose-h-multi-coco.pth\", \"inputs/checkpoints/vitpose\", \"vitpose-h-multi-coco.pth\")\n","fetch(f\"{base_g}/yolo/yolov8x.pt\", \"inputs/checkpoints/yolo\", \"yolov8x.pt\")\n","\n","!find inputs/checkpoints -type f | sort\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Helper: play an mp4 in the notebook\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import io, base64\n","from IPython.display import HTML, display\n","\n","def display_video(fn, max_w=720):\n","    from pathlib import Path\n","    fn = str(fn)\n","    assert Path(fn).exists(), fn\n","    data = base64.b64encode(open(fn, \"rb\").read()).decode(\"ascii\")\n","    return HTML(\n","        f'<video width=\"{max_w}\" controls>'\n","        f'<source src=\"data:video/mp4;base64,{data}\" type=\"video/mp4\" /></video>'\n","    )\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Smoke test on the bundled tennis clip (static cam)\n","\n","Uses `-s` so SimpleVO / identity camera is used. **Do not pass `--use_dpvo`. **\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["proj_root = \"/content/GVHMR\"\n","video_fn = f\"{proj_root}/docs/example_video/tennis.mp4\"\n","!python {proj_root}/tools/demo/demo.py --video={video_fn} -s\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","cands = list(Path(\"/content/GVHMR/outputs\").rglob(\"*incam_global_horiz.mp4\"))\n","print(\"\\n\".join(map(str, cands)))\n","if cands:\n","    display(display_video(cands[0]))\n","else:\n","    print(\"No preview video (pytorch3d missing is the usual cause). Check outputs/ for *.pt anyway.\")\n","    print(\"\\n\".join(map(str, Path(\"/content/GVHMR/outputs\").rglob(\"*\"))))\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Your exercise clip\n","\n","Upload the **same** mp4 you ran through `pipeline.py` on the Mac. Keep `STATIC_CAM = True` for phone-on-a-table / tripod footage.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import files\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","STATIC_CAM = True   # False only if the camera walks around the subject\n","\n","upload_dir = Path(\"/content/GVHMR/inputs/demo\")\n","upload_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","print(\"Choose your exercise mp4\")\n","uploaded = files.upload()\n","assert uploaded, \"No file uploaded.\"\n","name = next(iter(uploaded))\n","safe = name.replace(\" \", \"_\")\n","dst = upload_dir / safe\n","\n","data = uploaded[name]\n","if isinstance(data, (bytes, bytearray)):\n","    dst.write_bytes(data)\n","else:\n","    for cand in (Path.cwd() / name, Path(\"/content\") / name, Path(\"/content/GVHMR\") / name):\n","        if cand.exists() and cand.is_file():\n","            cand.replace(dst)\n","            break\n","\n","print(\"video\", dst, \"bytes\", dst.stat().st_size)\n","assert dst.exists() and dst.stat().st_size > 1000, dst\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","proj_root = \"/content/GVHMR\"\n","clips = sorted(Path(f\"{proj_root}/inputs/demo\").glob(\"*\"))\n","clips = [p for p in clips if p.suffix.lower() in {\".mp4\", \".mov\", \".webm\", \".mkv\"}]\n","assert clips, \"No clip in inputs/demo \— rerun the upload cell.\"\n","video_fn = clips[-1]\n","print(\"running\", video_fn)\n","flag = \"-s\" if STATIC_CAM else \"\"\n","!python {proj_root}/tools/demo/demo.py --video={video_fn} {flag}\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Export `gvhmr_smpl.npz` for the Mac pipeline\n","\n","`scripts/ingest_smpl.py` accepts `body_pose`, `global_orient`, `transl`, `betas`.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import torch\n","import numpy as np\n","from google.colab import files\n","\n","def to_np(x):\n","    if hasattr(x, \"detach\"):\n","        return x.detach().cpu().numpy()\n","    return np.asarray(x)\n","\n","pts = sorted(Path(\"/content/GVHMR/outputs\").rglob(\"*hmr4d_results*\")) + sorted(Path(\"/content/GVHMR/outputs\").rglob(\"*.pt\"))\n","pts = [p for p in pts if \"hmr4d\" in p.name.lower() or p.name.endswith(\"results.pt\")] or pts\n","print(\"candidate .pt files:\")\n","for p in pts:\n","    print(\" \", p, p.stat().st_size)\n","\n","assert pts, \"No result .pt \— demo.py failed earlier.\"\n","blob = torch.load(pts[0], map_location=\"cpu\", weights_only=False)\n","print(\"top keys:\", list(blob.keys()) if isinstance(blob, dict) else type(blob))\n","\n","params = None\n","if isinstance(blob, dict):\n","    for k in (\"smpl_params_global\", \"smpl_params_incam\", \"smpl_params\"):\n","        if k in blob:\n","            params = blob[k]\n","            print(\"using\", k)\n","            break\n","assert isinstance(params, dict), params\n","\n","pack = {}\n","alias = {\n","    \"body_pose\": (\"body_pose\", \"pose_body\"),\n","    \"global_orient\": (\"global_orient\", \"root_orient\"),\n","    \"transl\": (\"transl\", \"trans\"),\n","    \"betas\": (\"betas\",),\n",